WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.109
Film Courage: Is the director always the first
one on set?

00:00:04.109 --> 00:00:08.340
Would you ever see other crew members or actors
show up before you?

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.630
If so, what did that say about them?

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:24.160
Bill Duke: Some actors (I won’t mention
their names) but they are so involved in the

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.800
legitimacy of what they do.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.300
They are there before the crew and me.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:36.130
They just sit on the set and sit in the seat
and they know they’re…if it’s supposed

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:43.030
to be their bedroom, they’ll go in the bedroom
and touch the props, they’ll become familiar

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:47.741
with the pictures on the wall, what’s in
the closet?

00:00:47.741 --> 00:00:49.210
What kind of bed sheets are there?

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:50.730
What color are they?

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:55.190
How soft are they pillows and why those pillows
are that soft or why are they harder?

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.520
Is the blind closed are is it open?

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.740
Are there curtains on the wall?

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.340
And why was that color chosen for the sheet?

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.340
“Aaahh, okay…”

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:12.630
And they’re comfortable because it’s their
bedroom for the last 15 years.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:22.240
So sometimes they come to set two days before
and they just sit there and they become organically

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.820
ingrained.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:31.899
Some of the great actors have their own way
of becoming the truth of what they are supposed

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:32.899
to be.

00:01:32.899 --> 00:01:34.960
And I get there and they are like “Hey,
Bill.”

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.039
“What you doing here?”

00:01:36.039 --> 00:01:37.369
“You know what I’m doing?”

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:38.630
“You know what I’m doing…working.”

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:43.240
“I see and thank you, because I respect
that.”

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:48.490
They don’t just wait for you to tell them
what to do…they have their own because I’m

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:50.289
an actor, too.

00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:57.939
As you start surrendering to a character that
they author has written, it’s going to sound

00:01:57.939 --> 00:02:06.729
crazy but the character tries to live through
you if you accept him or her.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:14.280
I was playing a character once in a movie
(I forgot which one it was) and a week before

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:21.019
I was supposed to film, I started doing this
[makes noises with his mouth].

00:02:21.019 --> 00:02:24.430
Never done that in my life.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:28.319
My girlfriend at the time said “What are
you doing?”

00:02:28.319 --> 00:02:30.260
I said “What are you?”

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.980
She said “You’re going…[makes noises
with mouth].”

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.920
I said “No, I’m not.”

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.080
She said okay.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.579
Five minutes later I’m going…[makes noises
with his mouth].

00:02:39.579 --> 00:02:50.439
And that was the character coming through
me and so I put that in part of the film because

00:02:50.439 --> 00:02:57.540
I knew something that was being expressed
through that person.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:01.319
And it’s trust.

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:05.099
Trusting your instincts, yourself and your
talent.

00:03:05.099 --> 00:03:13.599
Film Courage: So if an actor once to do all
of those things, bring little idiosyncrasies,

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:19.769
ticks or show up three hours early, is something
they feel they need permission to do?

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:24.849
Because I could see a new actor wanting to
do those things but being scared because they

00:03:24.849 --> 00:03:27.189
don’t want to offend anybody or whatever.

00:03:27.189 --> 00:03:37.819
Bill Duke: If you’re a new actor and you
know what acting is and you have a good director,

00:03:37.819 --> 00:03:42.349
he’ll give you the permission that you need,
to be the best you can.

00:03:42.349 --> 00:03:57.260
Good directors…their ego…if I’m shooting
a scene with the star of the movie in a car

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:05.959
and we shot half this scene before lunch and
we shoot half the scene after lunch.

00:04:05.959 --> 00:04:17.280
And an intern, an assistant or a caterer comes
up to me and says “Hey, Bill, Bill…”

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.489
And I say “What?”

00:04:18.489 --> 00:04:24.300
“The license plate before you went to lunch
was straight but now it’s crooked.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.760
I don’t say “You’re the caterer.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.660
You’re an assistant.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:30.900
Mind your own business.”

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.600
That’s stupid!

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:41.060
I say “Thank you very much because I didn’t
see that.”

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:43.970
And I have my assistant go and straighten
up the license plate.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.490
You know why?

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:49.389
Because I still get directing credit.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.970
That person is no less than me.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.100
That person helped me out.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:59.139
But some people throw phones at….I don’t
understand these idiots.

00:04:59.139 --> 00:05:05.710
Throwing phones in people’s faces and this
royalty wave like they are superior to human

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:16.930
beings and an attitude of superiority like
people are…it’s annoying.

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:22.540
Because they are all going to die.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.550
They all bleed.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.760
And I do believe (I have no proof of course.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:36.110
I don’t want it) that when they all go to
the bathroom and do Number 2, they stink.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:41.550
And if they don’t…if they can prove they
don’t stink when they go to the bathroom,

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:46.550
I will worship them.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:53.880
But until that moment occurs, don’t come
to me with that crap.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.400
You understand?

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.590
You stink, I stink, we both stink.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.590
Cool.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.740
Do your damn job.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:01.740
Simple.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.580
Film Courage: We’re going to assume that
they stink.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:12.199
Bill Duke: If you’re asking me if I’m
going to the bathroom, I’m not.

00:06:12.199 --> 00:06:16.009
Film Courage: We will air on the side of caution.

00:06:16.009 --> 00:06:17.110
Bill Duke: Great caution!

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.740
Film Courage: Nice pun, too.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:19.740
Air.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:20.740
Bill Duke: Air.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:25.199
See I like that what she said.

00:06:25.199 --> 00:06:26.110
Air…Air.

